<invention-title id="d2e43">Allocating idle graphics processing unit capacity of client devices to remote workloads</invention-title>
<us-parties>
<us-applicants><us-applicant sequence="00" app-type="applicant"><addressbook><orgname>Example Systems Corporation</orgname></addressbook></us-applicant></us-applicants>
<inventors><inventor sequence="00"><addressbook><last-name>Lindqvist</last-name><first-name>Mara</first-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors>
</us-parties>
</us-bibliographic-data-application>
<abstract id="abstract"><p>An operating system service detects when a personal computer is idle and
offers its unused GPU capacity to a scheduler that dispatches distributed
workloads, reclaiming the GPU when the user returns.</p></abstract>
<claims id="claims"><claim id="CLM-00001" num="00001"><claim-text>1. A method comprising detecting an idle state of a client device, advertising spare GPU capacity to a scheduler, and executing a remote workload on the GPU until user activity resumes.</claim-text></claim></claims>
</us-patent-application>
